l solutions to residential, commercial, industrial, and municipal customers in the United States, Canada, Western Europe, and internationally. It offers collection services, including picking up and transporting waste and recyclable materials from where it was generated to a transfer station, recovery facility, or disposal site; owns and operates transfer stations; and owns, develops, and operates landfill gas-to-energy facilities that produce renewable electricity and renewable natural gas. It also operates materials processing and commodities recycling services, including cardboard, paper, glass, metals, plastics, construction and demolition materials, and other recycling commodities are recovered for resale or redirected for other purposes; markets and resells recycling commodities; recycling brokerage services, such as managing the marketing of recyclable materials for third parties; and other strategic business solutions. In addition, the company collects recyclable food and yard waste, as well as markets and sells mulch, compost, soil amendments, and renewable energy; offers remediation and construction, and industrial waste services; and manages and markets fly ash. Further, it provides Regulated Waste and Compliance Services (RWCS), which offers compliance programs, as well as collection, processing, and disposal of regulated and specialized waste, including medical, pharmaceutical, and hazardous waste; and Secure Information Destruction (SID) services that include the collection of personal and confidential information for secure destruction and recycling of sorted office paper. The company was formerly known as USA Waste Services, Inc. and changed its name to Waste Management, Inc. in 1998. Waste Management, Inc. was founded in 1968 and is based in Houston, Texas.","ceo_bio":"Mr. James C. Fish Jr. | CEO & Director | Age 63 | Compensation: $4.2M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 60K people. Revenue per employee of $417K ranks in the above the sector median among Industrials peers. Each employee generates $47K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $3K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 10\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["Waste Management, Inc. is a large-cap industrials business with a $97.0B market cap on $25.2B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +9% over the past three years and +7% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 12% against a 7% cost of capital, a 5-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it.","The business throws off $2.8B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 11 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 2.23\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 3.2\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and interest coverage runs at 4.6\u00d7.","Shareholder yield is only 1.4%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 1.5\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Trading near 52-week highs \u2014 the market has already recognised the story","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.39712583245706506},{"text":"Insiders are overwhelmingly selling (100% sell ratio) \u2014 the people who know the business want less of it","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","ratio":0.0},{"text":"Industrials sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 6% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cyclicality and capital intensity \u2014 order books turn on a dime, and the heavy fixed cost base that creates the moat also magnifies the downturn.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Supply chain reshoring costs and labour shortages \u2014 onshoring mandates raise capex requirements while a shrinking skilled-labour pool inflates operating costs.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 8% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","27 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Waste Management (WM) Stock Looks Reasonably Priced On Cash Flow","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/waste-management-wm-stock-looks-200654602.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794600414.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.168,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Waste Management (WM), Is There More To Its Latest Update?","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/waste-management-wm-more-latest-151103076.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794582663.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.026,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"WM Stock Jumps 13% in 6 Months: Here's What You Should Know","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3029574/wm-stock-jumps-13-in-6-months-here-s-what-you-should-know?cid=CS-ZC-FT-analyst_blog%7Cprice_surge_%2F_plunge-3029574","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794578640.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Waste Management, Inc. $WM Sto